---
import { site } from '../data/site';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const email = site.contact.email;
const githubPrivacy = 'https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement';
const googlePrivacy = 'https://policies.google.com/privacy';
const dpfList = 'https://www.dataprivacyframework.gov/list';
const adequacyDecision = 'https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2023/1795/oj';
const authority = 'https://www.dsb.gv.at/';
---

<Base title="Privacy" noindex>
  <main id="main" class="in stub">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        This site sets no cookies, uses no analytics or tracking, and has no embedded third-party content. Fonts, images
        and video come from the same host as the pages. Two things still involve personal data: hosting, and any email
        you send me.
      </p>

      <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
      <p>
        {site.name}, Linz, Austria. Email: <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
        You can also reach me on <a href={site.links.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        This site is hosted on GitHub Pages, a service of GitHub, and delivered through the Fastly content delivery
        network. To show you a page, these services process technical data such as your IP address, the page requested
        and the time of the request. GitHub states that it logs each visitor's IP address for security purposes, whether
        or not the visitor has a GitHub account. I do not receive these logs. GitHub does not publish how long it keeps
        them. See the <a href={githubPrivacy}>GitHub Privacy Statement</a>.
      </p>
      <p>The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. The legitimate interest is delivering this site reliably and securely.</p>

      <h2>Transfer to the United States</h2>
      <p>
        GitHub, Inc. is based in the United States, so your data may be processed there. GitHub states that it complies
        with the <a href={dpfList}>EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework</a>, which is covered by the European Commission's
        adequacy decision <a href={adequacyDecision}>(EU) 2023/1795</a>, and that it also relies on the Commission's
        standard contractual clauses.
      </p>

      <h2>Email</h2>
      <p>
        If you email me, I process your address, your message and any details you include, in order to reply. The legal
        basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR, my legitimate interest in answering you, or Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR if your message
        concerns a possible job or contract.
      </p>
      <p>
        My mailbox is hosted by Gmail, a service of Google Ireland Limited, Gordon House, Barrow Street, Dublin 4,
        Ireland, which handles this data under the <a href={googlePrivacy}>Google Privacy Policy</a>. I delete messages
        no later than 12 months after our last contact, unless they are part of an employment relationship or I need
        them for a legal claim.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask me for access to your data, and for its rectification, erasure, restriction or transfer. A short
        email is enough. I can only act on data I hold, which means your emails and not GitHub's logs. For those, please
        contact GitHub.
      </p>
      <p>Where I rely on legitimate interests, you can ask how I weighed them against your interests.</p>
      <p>
        <strong>Right to object:</strong> you can object at any time to processing based on Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR, on grounds
        relating to your particular situation.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can complain to the Austrian Data Protection Authority (Österreichische Datenschutzbehörde), Barichgasse
        40-42, 1030 Vienna, <a href="mailto:dsb@dsb.gv.at">dsb@dsb.gv.at</a>, <a href={authority}>dsb.gv.at</a>, or to the
        authority where you live or work.
      </p>

      <h2>Other notes</h2>
      <p>
        You do not have to give me any data to read this site, though the technical data above is needed to deliver it.
        If you want a reply, I need your email address. I make no automated decisions about you. Links to other sites
        send nothing until you click them; those sites then apply their own privacy rules.
      </p>
      <p>Last updated: November 6, 2026</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
